## Three wizards (families, from English): generated by spec_backend.py (WorldSpec, path B: Lean description, Python rules) from the instructor statements.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##  1. Three wizards, A, B and C, sit where each can see the others but not himself.
##  2. Each has a spot on his forehead that is either white or black.
##  3. They are told that at least one spot is white.
##  4. They are asked in turn, A, then B, then C, whether they know the colour of their own spot.
##  5. Each can reason about what the others would have concluded from what they see and from the answers so far.
##  6. In this instance B and C have white spots and A has a black spot.
##  7. The goal is that a wizard correctly states the colour of his own spot.
##
## Assumption ledger:
##   A-WZ1: The eight possible patterns of spots are world objects (w-bww: A black, B white, C white); spot(c, w, colour) gives each wizard's colour in each world; view-mate(c, w, w2) holds when w2 differs from w only in c's own spot (what c cannot see). The actual world is w-bww.
##   A-WZ2: "B and C start marked, A unmarked" in the description is read as B and C white and A black (marked = the colour the announcement is about).
##   A-WZ3: Knowledge is explicit: knows-at(c, w, r) holds when, in world w at turn r, no world c cannot tell from w is still possible. Derived relations use negation only in their definitions; operators test them positively.
##   A-WZ4: The announcement and each turn are operators that rule out worlds (out-at(w, turn)). A world is live at turn r if it was not ruled out at an earlier turn. A stage number keeps the order; turn objects carry their number and asks(turn, wizard) says who is asked (A, B, C in that order).
##   A-WZ5: A turn records the asked wizard's answer in the actual world: if he knows, he states his colour (says(c, colour), the colour of his spot in the actual world, so it is correct). Every world where he would have answered differently is ruled out, since all hear the answer.
##   A-WZ6: The goal is that some wizard has stated his colour. With A black, B and C white, A and B do not know and C states white at the third turn.
## Matching hints for learned rules (World-Conventions L3-095, L11-009): many-valued attributes, sized from the initial world.
production optimize-attribute object 19
production optimize-attribute spot 24
production optimize-attribute view-mate 24
production optimize-attribute actual 2
production optimize-attribute asks 3
production optimize-attribute out-at 2
production optimize-attribute says 2


## Propose initialize-wizards when its conditions below hold.
sp {wizards*propose*initialize-wizards
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-wizards ^task-operator false)
}

sp {wizards*apply*initialize-wizards
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-wizards ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name wizards ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <k-a> <k-b> <k-c> <k-white> <k-black> <k-w-www> <k-w-wwb> <k-w-wbw> <k-w-wbb> <k-w-bww> <k-w-bwb> <k-w-bbw> <k-w-bbb> <k-told> <k-turn-a> <k-turn-b> <k-turn-c> <k-talk> <k-task>)
   (<k-a> ^object-handle a ^anchored true ^type wizard ^name a ^static true)
   (<k-b> ^object-handle b ^anchored true ^type wizard ^name b ^static true)
   (<k-c> ^object-handle c ^anchored true ^type wizard ^name c ^static true)
   (<k-white> ^object-handle white ^anchored true ^type colour ^name white ^static true)
   (<k-black> ^object-handle black ^anchored true ^type colour ^name black ^static true)
   (<k-w-www> ^object-handle w-www ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-www ^static true)
   (<k-w-wwb> ^object-handle w-wwb ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-wwb ^static true)
   (<k-w-wbw> ^object-handle w-wbw ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-wbw ^static true)
   (<k-w-wbb> ^object-handle w-wbb ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-wbb ^static true)
   (<k-w-bww> ^object-handle w-bww ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-bww ^static true)
   (<k-w-bwb> ^object-handle w-bwb ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-bwb ^static true)
   (<k-w-bbw> ^object-handle w-bbw ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-bbw ^static true)
   (<k-w-bbb> ^object-handle w-bbb ^anchored true ^type world ^name w-bbb ^static true)
   (<k-told> ^object-handle told ^anchored true ^type turn ^name told ^n 0 ^static true)
   (<k-turn-a> ^object-handle turn-a ^anchored true ^type turn ^name turn-a ^n 1 ^static true)
   (<k-turn-b> ^object-handle turn-b ^anchored true ^type turn ^name turn-b ^n 2 ^static true)
   (<k-turn-c> ^object-handle turn-c ^anchored true ^type turn ^name turn-c ^n 3 ^static true)
   (<k-talk> ^object-handle talk ^anchored true ^type stage ^name talk ^step 0)
   (<k-task> ^object-handle task ^anchored true ^type task)
   (<ds> ^desired-count 1 ^desired <d1>)
   (<d1> ^object <d1-o>)
   (<d1-o> ^object-handle task ^goal-met true)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-1>)
   (<rel-1> ^argument1 <k-a> ^argument2 <k-w-www> ^argument3 <k-white>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-2>)
   (<rel-2> ^argument1 <k-b> ^argument2 <k-w-www> ^argument3 <k-white>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-3>)
   (<rel-3> ^argument1 <k-c> ^argument2 <k-w-www> ^argument3 <k-white>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-4>)
   (<rel-4> ^argument1 <k-a> ^argument2 <k-w-wwb> ^argument3 <k-white>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-5>)
   (<rel-5> ^argument1 <k-b> ^argument2 <k-w-wwb> ^argument3 <k-white>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-6>)
   (<rel-6> ^argument1 <k-c> ^argument2 <k-w-wwb> ^argument3 <k-black>)
   (<w> ^spot <rel-7>)
   (<rel-7> ^argument1 <k-a> ^argument2 <k-w-wbw> ^argument3 <k-white>)
